1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,680
If your knee replacement
still

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,470
feels tight two years
later

3
00:00:03,470 --> 00:00:05,970
and every X-ray comes back
perfect,

4
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:07,220
there is one thing nobody

5
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:08,720
in that room is checking.

6
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,360
I found it the hard way,

7
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:11,320
and it took my wife

8
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:12,890
two years of her life.

9
00:00:12,890 --> 00:00:14,670
She is seventy-one.

10
00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:16,270
Worked outside her whole
life,

11
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:18,260
never sat still a day.

12
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:19,890
Then she had the knee
done,

13
00:00:19,890 --> 00:00:21,710
and she started moving
like

14
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:23,100
a much older woman.

15
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:24,910
The knee was tight from
the minute

16
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:26,540
she stood up in the
morning.

17
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:28,770
Like a band cinched around
it.

18
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:30,030
By evening she was taking

19
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:31,720
the stairs one at a time,

20
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:33,300
both hands on the rail.

21
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,250
And it woke her at two

22
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:36,280
in the morning, every
night.

23
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:36,950
I know,

24
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:38,810
because I was lying right
there.

25
00:00:38,810 --> 00:00:40,060
She'd be up at two,

26
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,130
then four,

27
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:42,330
shifting the leg around

28
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:43,400
trying to find a position

29
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:44,490
that didn't ache.

30
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:46,770
She wasn't tired from
doing too much.

31
00:00:46,770 --> 00:00:47,970
She was tired from a knee

32
00:00:47,970 --> 00:00:50,380
that never once let her
stay asleep.

33
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:52,940
She stopped volunteering
to walk the dog.

34
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:55,050
Stopped going to the
grandkids' games.

35
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:57,250
Started doing the
parking-lot math before

36
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,360
she'd even get out of the
car.

37
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:00,900
So of course she went back
in.

38
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:01,560
Over and over.

39
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:02,740
Her surgeon.

40
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:03,730
Her primary.

41
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:05,840
Four sets of X-rays on
that knee.

42
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:06,650
Scans.

43
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:07,860
Bloodwork.

44
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:08,990
An infection test.

45
00:01:08,990 --> 00:01:10,260
The whole list.

46
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:11,510
And every single time,

47
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:12,600
for two years,

48
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:13,940
the same answers.

49
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:15,500
"The replacement looks
great."

50
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:16,850
"Alignment is good."

51
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:19,300
"Probably just doing a
little too much."

52
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:20,580
"Try more therapy."

53
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:22,310
"Give it another six
months."

54
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:23,970
She was already two years
out,

55
00:01:23,970 --> 00:01:25,200
and they handed her the
same

56
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:26,440
six months again.

57
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,040
Then they sent

58
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,730
her for a nerve block.

59
00:01:28,730 --> 00:01:29,690
For about three weeks

60
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:30,820
the knee went quiet.

61
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:32,110
She thought that was it.

62
00:01:32,110 --> 00:01:33,470
Then it came back exactly

63
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:34,650
the way it left.

64
00:01:34,650 --> 00:01:35,920
And the tightness

65
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:38,060
never went anywhere at
all.

66
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:39,820
That block quieted the
signal.

67
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,700
It never touched the thing
sending it.

68
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,460
That was the point I got
angry.

69
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:44,490
I was watching a woman

70
00:01:44,490 --> 00:01:46,490
who did every exercise,

71
00:01:46,490 --> 00:01:47,780
went to every appointment,

72
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,460
took everything they gave
her,

73
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:50,500
and got no better.

74
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,370
Not once.

75
00:01:51,370 --> 00:01:52,330
So I started reading.

76
00:01:52,330 --> 00:01:53,460
Not the surgical stuff.

77
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:54,610
The tissue research.

78
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:55,690
The work that never comes

79
00:01:55,690 --> 00:01:56,940
up at the appointment.

80
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:58,430
And I found the thing
nobody had

81
00:01:58,430 --> 00:02:00,440
said to her in two full
years.

82
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:01,800
They cut through it.

83
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,170
To put the new joint in,

84
00:02:03,170 --> 00:02:04,560
they have to work through
the living

85
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,340
tissue wrapped around the
knee.

86
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:07,620
A sleeve of muscle,

87
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:08,940
capsule and lining,

88
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:10,720
packed tight around the
joint.

89
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:11,730
All of it disturbed

90
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:12,890
on the way in.

91
00:02:12,890 --> 00:02:14,950
Afterward, that tissue
swells.

92
00:02:14,950 --> 00:02:16,950
At first that's completely
normal.

93
00:02:16,950 --> 00:02:18,290
It's what tissue does.

94
00:02:18,290 --> 00:02:19,610
When it settles down,

95
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:20,730
there's room again.

96
00:02:20,730 --> 00:02:21,900
The knee bends.

97
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,100
Everything moves.

98
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,070
But in some people

99
00:02:24,070 --> 00:02:26,050
it never fully settles.

100
00:02:26,050 --> 00:02:28,590
And swollen tissue takes
up room.

101
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:30,740
Think about your foot
inside a shoe.

102
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:32,560
The shoe never changed
size.

103
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,670
Your foot did.

104
00:02:33,670 --> 00:02:36,300
Everything goes tight,
cramped, squeezed.

105
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,910
Her implant was fine.

106
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:38,870
Her problem was never

107
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:40,740
the metal or the plastic.

108
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:42,050
Her problem was that there

109
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:43,850
was no room left in there.

110
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:45,230
Bend it, and that swollen

111
00:02:45,230 --> 00:02:46,930
tissue gets compressed.

112
00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:49,230
Straighten it, and it
pulls tight.

113
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:51,660
That is what the tightness
actually is.

114
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:53,410
Not a part that failed.

115
00:02:53,410 --> 00:02:54,540
A room that got smaller

116
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:55,560
while the joint inside

117
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,280
it stayed the same size.

118
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:59,000
And once you see that, you
understand

119
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,750
why the nerve block didn't
hold.

120
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:02,070
It turned down the alarm.

121
00:03:02,070 --> 00:03:04,200
The swelling doing the
squeezing was still

122
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,970
sitting right where it
was.

123
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:06,760
Here is the part

124
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,570
that made my blood boil.

125
00:03:08,570 --> 00:03:10,240
None of this is a secret.

126
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,810
It's in the research.

127
00:03:11,810 --> 00:03:13,240
But the appointment she
kept going

128
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,700
to was built to answer one
question.

129
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,790
Is the implant sound.

130
00:03:17,790 --> 00:03:19,570
And the answer was always
yes.

131
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:21,600
A good X-ray ends the
appointment.

132
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:23,790
It doesn't end the pain.

133
00:03:23,790 --> 00:03:25,290
There is no test for
tight.

134
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:26,980
Nothing on that scan
measures how much

135
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:28,310
room is left in there.

136
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:29,130
So you can walk out

137
00:03:29,130 --> 00:03:31,020
with a perfect X-ray in
your hand

138
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:32,170
and the exact same knee

139
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:33,390
you walked in with.

140
00:03:33,390 --> 00:03:34,650
So I kept reading,

141
00:03:34,650 --> 00:03:36,120
looking for anything that
calms

142
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:37,280
that tissue down

143
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:38,880
instead of numbing it.

144
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:40,990
It came down to four
things.

145
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:43,240
660 nanometers.

146
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:43,840
Red light,

147
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,630
working nearer the
surface,

148
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:47,760
where the tissue is most
irritated.

149
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,000
850 nanometers.

150
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,980
Near-infrared, reaching
deeper,

151
00:03:51,980 --> 00:03:53,390
down where the tissue
wraps

152
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:54,900
around the joint itself.

153
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:55,670
This is the one

154
00:03:55,670 --> 00:03:57,280
that matters most here.

155
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,270
Both wavelengths running
together.

156
00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:01,620
Not one and then the
other.

157
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:02,700
Both at once,

158
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,100
the whole session.

159
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:06,440
And twenty minutes,
sitting down.

160
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:08,060
No stretching it farther,

161
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:09,890
no pushing through
anything.

162
00:04:09,890 --> 00:04:10,900
You sit,

163
00:04:10,900 --> 00:04:12,760
and the light does the
work.

164
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,430
In a randomized trial,

165
00:04:14,430 --> 00:04:15,770
people who had light
therapy

166
00:04:15,770 --> 00:04:17,130
after a knee replacement

167
00:04:17,130 --> 00:04:19,420
had less pain, less
swelling,

168
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:21,200
and better early movement.

169
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,700
It just isn't on the list

170
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:24,490
of things that appointment
checks.

171
00:04:24,490 --> 00:04:26,380
So I talked her into
trying it.

172
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:27,850
And here was the problem.

173
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:28,860
The only place near us

174
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:30,190
doing it was a clinic.

175
00:04:30,190 --> 00:04:31,800
Twenty minutes on a table,

176
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,100
then drive home.

177
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,730
Two hundred dollars a
session.

178
00:04:34,730 --> 00:04:36,340
Insurance covers none of
it.

179
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:37,100
Booking it.

180
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:38,130
Driving it.

181
00:04:38,130 --> 00:04:39,780
Sitting in the waiting
room.

182
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:40,710
And the whole point

183
00:04:40,710 --> 00:04:42,380
of this is that you do

184
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:44,150
it every single day.

185
00:04:44,150 --> 00:04:44,770
So I bought one

186
00:04:44,770 --> 00:04:46,150
for the house instead.

187
00:04:46,150 --> 00:04:47,610
Two of them, actually.

188
00:04:47,610 --> 00:04:49,600
Only her right knee was
replaced,

189
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,940
but she'd favored that leg

190
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:52,090
for two years,

191
00:04:52,090 --> 00:04:52,880
and the left one had

192
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,640
been carrying the
difference.

193
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:55,830
It's called the KenRelief

194
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:57,480
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

195
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,890
It straps around the
joint,

196
00:04:58,890 --> 00:05:00,470
so the light sits flat
against

197
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:02,110
the skin the whole
session,

198
00:05:02,110 --> 00:05:04,270
instead of a panel across
the room

199
00:05:04,270 --> 00:05:06,410
or a wand you have to
hold.

200
00:05:06,410 --> 00:05:07,870
Both wavelengths together,

201
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:10,800
660 and 850.

202
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:12,540
Two hundred forty lights.

203
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:14,070
And when I dug into who
they

204
00:05:14,070 --> 00:05:16,030
built it for, it was
people

205
00:05:16,030 --> 00:05:18,520
who had already had the
replacement.

206
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:19,810
Not arthritis.

207
00:05:19,810 --> 00:05:21,960
Not sore muscles after the
gym.

208
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,130
The knee that got replaced

209
00:05:23,130 --> 00:05:24,770
and stayed tight anyway.

210
00:05:24,770 --> 00:05:26,370
She used it every night,

211
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:27,710
in her chair.

212
00:05:27,710 --> 00:05:28,970
After about three weeks,

213
00:05:28,970 --> 00:05:31,190
the tightness started
letting go.

214
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,110
After a month,

215
00:05:32,110 --> 00:05:33,300
she was taking the stairs

216
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:34,790
without the handrail.

217
00:05:34,790 --> 00:05:37,020
After two months she was
sleeping through,

218
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:38,570
and walking the dog again.

219
00:05:38,570 --> 00:05:39,630
And I watched her stop

220
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,290
doing the parking-lot
math.

221
00:05:41,290 --> 00:05:42,410
She just parked and got

222
00:05:42,410 --> 00:05:44,000
out like anyone else.

223
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,650
She's been using

224
00:05:44,650 --> 00:05:46,100
it for six months now.

225
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,490
The tightness is gone.

226
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:49,540
The two a.m. is gone.

227
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:50,530
She went to every one

228
00:05:50,530 --> 00:05:52,280
of the grandkids' games
this spring.

229
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,270
One time,

230
00:05:53,270 --> 00:05:54,860
unlimited sessions.

231
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:57,210
Ten thousand people are
using it now.

232
00:05:57,210 --> 00:05:58,590
No prescription.

233
00:05:58,590 --> 00:05:59,960
No appointment.

234
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,300
Nothing to book.

235
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,620
Twenty minutes a day,

236
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:03,680
and that's it.

237
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,360
Right now it's 50 percent
off,

238
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:07,310
which comes to under 80
dollars.

239
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:09,570
Less than one visit to
that clinic.

240
00:06:09,570 --> 00:06:12,190
And it comes with a 90-day
guarantee.

241
00:06:12,190 --> 00:06:14,160
Use it daily for three
months,

242
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,190
and if your knee isn't
better

243
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:17,200
you get every penny back.

244
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,170
No forms.

245
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:19,370
No questions.

246
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:20,980
You don't even send it
back.

247
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:22,900
So here's where you
actually are.

248
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:24,930
You can keep waiting to
feel better,

249
00:06:24,930 --> 00:06:26,020
with a real chance

250
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:27,770
you simply never do.

251
00:06:27,770 --> 00:06:28,960
Or you can spend a few

252
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,410
weeks calming the tissue

253
00:06:30,410 --> 00:06:31,740
that has been swollen
since

254
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,580
the day they closed you
up.

255
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,810
Because nobody is going

256
00:06:34,810 --> 00:06:36,490
to call you about this.

257
00:06:36,490 --> 00:06:38,670
That appointment already
ended.

258
00:06:38,670 --> 00:06:39,610
It ended the day

259
00:06:39,610 --> 00:06:41,720
